  "question": {
    "text": "In a binomial distribution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, the sum and product of the mean &amp; variance are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> respectively, then find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to :-"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>51</mn></math>",
